        "instructions": [
          {
            "id": 243732,
            "primary_message": "Wash, dry, peel, and trim beets. Medium dice, transfer to a large pot, and cover with hot water (from the tap). Cover and bring to a boil over high heat.",
            "secondary_message": "2 medium beets"
          },
          {
            "id": 243733,
            "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the remaining fresh produce.",
            "secondary_message": "1 lb sweet potato\n2 lemons\n1 bunch kale"
          },
          {
            "id": 243734,
            "primary_message": "Peel, trim, and medium dice sweet potatoes; place in a medium bowl and set aside.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 243735,
            "primary_message": "Once the water in the pot is boiling, reduce to a simmer and cook until beets are starting to soften, about 10 minutes. Add sweet potatoes and cook until veggies are soft, 10-12 minutes more.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 243736,
            "primary_message": "While the beets are cooking, juice lemons into another medium bowl. Add oil, Dijon, salt, and pepper; whisk to combine the dressing and set aside.",
            "secondary_message": "4 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n4 tsp Dijon mustard\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
          },
          {
            "id": 243737,
            "primary_message": "Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 243738,
            "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, pat the chicken dry with paper towels and place on a cutting board. Holding a knife parallel to the cutting board, cut the chicken in half horizontally to form thin cutlets. Season with salt and pepper on both sides.",
            "secondary_message": "1 ½ lb chicken breasts, boneless skinless\n1 tsp salt\n½ tsp black pepper"
          },
          {
            "id": 243739,
            "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add cutlets to the skillet and pan-fry until cooked through and golden brown, 3-4 minutes per side. Remove to a plate and loosely cover with aluminum foil.",
            "secondary_message": "4 tsp extra virgin olive oil"
          },
          {
            "id": 243740,
            "primary_message": "Meanwhile, using a clean cutting board, fold kale leaves in half lengthwise and slice off the stems. Chop or tear leaves into bite-sized pieces and add to the bowl with the dressing; toss to combine the salad and set aside.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 243741,
            "primary_message": "Peel and mince garlic and shallots.",
            "secondary_message": "2 cloves garlic\n2 shallots"
          },
          {
            "id": 243742,
            "primary_message": "Return the skillet (with cooking juices), to medium heat; add garlic, shallot, and thyme. Cook, stirring occasionally, until shallot has softened, 2-3 minutes.",
            "secondary_message": "1 tsp thyme, dried"
          },
          {
            "id": 243743,
            "primary_message": "While the shallot is cooking, cut cream cheese into small pieces.",
            "secondary_message": "1 (8 oz) block cream cheese"
          },
          {
            "id": 243744,
            "primary_message": "Add cream cheese and water to the skillet; stir until melted and combined, 1-2 minutes (if needed, add additional water, 1 tablespoon at a time, to reach a saucy consistency). Return chicken to the skillet, along with any accumulated juices; stir to combine the chicken and sauce. Remove from heat.",
            "secondary_message": "¼ cup water"
          },
          {
            "id": 243745,
            "primary_message": "When the beet and sweet potato are ready, drain in a colander and return to the pot; add salt and pepper, then use a hand (or regular blender) to purée until smooth. (Add water, if needed, a few tablespoons at a time, to reach desired consistency.)",
            "secondary_message": "½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
          },
          {
            "id": 243746,
            "primary_message": "To serve, divide sweet potato-beet mash, chicken, sauce, and salad between plates. Enjoy!",
            "secondary_message": null
          }
        ],
